  "notes": "Francophone subsystem (about 85% of primary pupils). Cameroon's anglophone subsystem, dominant in the North-West and South-West, names its classes Class 1–6, Form 1–5, Lower and Upper Sixth and is a separate file, CM-ANG. Primary is in three levels: Niveau I (SIL, CP), II (CE1, CE2), III (CM1, CM2). The BEPC ends 3e, the Probatoire is taken in 1ère and the Baccalauréat in Terminale. Technical secondary also runs 4 + 3 years."
